  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "X[k] = sum over n of x[n] * exp(-2*pi*i*k*n/size), for one k only",
        "A transform gives every frequency; here only one is wanted",
        "The angle comes from the bin nearest the frequency you asked for"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "s[n] = x[n] + coefficient*s[n-1] - s[n-2], with coefficient = 2*cos(w)",
        "real = s[n] - s[n-1]*cos(w) and imaginary = s[n-1]*sin(w)",
        "The sum is never worked out; a filter with two poles gives the same answer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it costs you",
      "items": [
        "One multiplication and two additions for each sample",
        "The whole state is two values and two constants, and no block is held",
        "Above about log2(size) frequencies, a transform costs less than this"
      ]
    }
  ]
